 "details": {
  "title": "How Deep Is the Ocean",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Perry Como’s record: B♭ minor and D♭ (C minor and E♭ for the trumpet), about 78, then up a half step to D for the last section after the guitar’s interlude. Concert B♭3 to D♭5. It keeps the notes he sings where the page names them: his climb to F, the A♭ he holds over F minor (major 7), his G♭ over B7, his D♭ at the end, G and F♯ over C9, and where the guitar’s chords would rub the lead sheet’s note it takes the chord’s: F♭ over G diminished, D over A♭7♯11. It rests while the guitar plays alone, opens with the tune’s turn over the intro’s chords, and closes over D major 9 and G minor 6, B♭ falling to A.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Irving Berlin (1932)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, with Perry Como’s notes where the Fret Finder page names them, on that page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "B♭ minor and D♭ major concert, then D major (C minor and E♭, then E, for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, A B A C, guitar interlude, the last section up a half step, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (hd-full-guitar.mp3), 2:56"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The page numbers its three intro bars Intro 1 to 3, so its bar 1 is bar 4 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
